  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_025, a multimodal multiprofile model using PCA, ViT, avgpool, and weighted fusion. RNA-only evidence shows PCA with avgpool is strong, but scGPT has only been tested in RNA-only mode, where it underperformed PCA. It is therefore unclear whether a learned RNA encoder can help in the best multimodal setting. config_049 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scGPT while keeping the promising multiprofile, ViT, avgpool, and weighted fusion settings fixed, cleanly isolating the RNA representation effect. This is a high-value next experiment because it either identifies a better RNA encoder for the current best pipeline or confirms PCA as the preferred RNA representation under a limited budget."
